We all come into the living room with hot cups of chai.
Asha, Rohan, Priya, and I stand near the open doors of the balcony.
We do not go outside.
Outside, the fiercest rain of the season has started.
The wind is blowing very fast.
The rain is falling horizontally, and it is crashing heavily on our neighborhood.
But we are standing safely inside, completely dry.
Rohan looks at the dark sky and takes a sip of tea.
He says, "Maya, the Mumbai monsoon has truly arrived today."
Priya laughs and agrees with him.
"Yes, I never saw such intense rain," she says.
Asha points to the street below.
She tells us, "Last week, it rained very gently."
"But today the weather has completely changed."
I watch the heavy raindrops crashing against the balcony railing.
I smile and look at my friends.
"I love this intense weather," I tell them.
"I never saw such rain in Mexico."
We stand there quietly, drinking our hot tea and watching the rain.
This is a perfect way to celebrate my birthday.
